  {
    "id": "69edc6cc-bc04-4a86-b8a4-c3bd3ba64e13",
    "title": "Launchpad Program Online Briefing",
    "content": "Dann Ombao - CEO, Co-founder<div>Rafa - Senior Software Engineer</div><div>Skills needed in Whitecloak according to Rafa:</div><div><ol><li>Be Open to Adapting</li><li>Growth is not only becoming better technically, but also communicate and help others as well</li><li>You do not have to go through alone</li></ol><div>Take the most out of the opportunity to learn from the challenges.</div></div><div><br></div><div>Sandra - Founding Growth Lead</div><div>- you can enjoy the culture and growth in the company</div><div>- be attentive, know the product well, learn everything you can\n\nProduct Analyst Role</div><div>- emerging role, no traditional path yet</div><div>asks who it is for, what people are trying to accomplish, where they get stuck, what's worth improving</div><div>how:</div><div><ol><li>understand the experience from diff. perspective</li><li>decide what needs attention. assess what problems matter and why.</li><li>translate understanding into a requirement</li><li>make the case to others; tell why you recommendation is</li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">analyze</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">assess</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">act</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">articulate</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">advance</span></li></ol>The Challenge</div><div><ul><li>all candidates work onsite on the assigned tickets</li><li>do nto need to know everything on day 1: form understanding of the product and the problem</li><li>15-min consultation; up to 3 clarification emails </li><li>outputs: documentation, requirements + prototype, presentation</li></ul><div>all project materials will be given at 10am on Sep 21</div></div><div>how reviewed:</div><div>product understanding - 30</div><div>reqs quality - 30</div><div>analysis and product judgement - 20</div><div>documentation - 20</div><div><br></div><div>minimum - 70%</div><div>demo day - oct 1 (8-5pm)</div><div><br></div><div>few tips: </div><div>1. understand before you build</div><div>2. use AI with intention</div><div>3. look around, explore the product, do your research</div><div>4. ask questions</div><div>5. bring your own thinking</div><div>6. make your thinking visible: share not only what you recommend, but how you arrived there.</div><div><br></div><div>allowance: 5k, 2 weeks after</div><div>9:30am on monday, free lunch, stocked pantry, conducive work environment</div><div><br></div><div>SMART CASUAL</div><div>BE READY TO EXPLORE</div><div>will be working on whitecloak product</div><div>plan around the submission deadlines 21 and 25 11:59am</div><div><br></div><div>MAKE THE MOST OUT OF THE 5 DAYS</div><div><br></div><div>working on the same project, but individual activity</div><div>you can work around at home, 21-25 is mandatory onsite 10-4pm</div><div>nda will be sent today + deck</div><div><br></div><div>how many applicants to move on from demo day, based on performance. only on quality of the output. this is you vs you. </div><div>one of the requirements is a prototype</div><div><br></div><div>maximize all tools, even AI. use it responsibly.</div><div><br></div><div>working protype on the 25th</div><div><br></div><div>use claude design for the prototype. tip: prototype it needs ot eb able to display the solution, for a certain ticket or issue</div><div><br></div><div>working site, given after the NDA. </div><div>ideal starting date: october 5th</div><div><br></div><div>number of people who will be accepted is open</div><div><br></div><div>STRICTLY CLAUDE DESIGN FOR THE PROTOTYPE</div><div><br></div><div>deck will be sent in the email after the meeting.</div><div><br></div><div>weekend: rest up and sleep earlyT</div><div><br></div>",
    "color": "#F0D58A",
    "updatedAt": 1789720436178,
    "alwaysOnTop": false
  },
  {
    "id": "2af0ebe9-b32f-486a-9ad8-fe5d3ec0c3e9",
    "title": "FREE TABBIN NOTES!",
    "content": "This note contains my checklist before I publish Tabbin Notes online. <div><i>Target Date: September 16, 2026</i><div><ol><li><strike>Fix Initial Fixes and Features</strike></li><li>Clean and Detailed Documentation</li><li>Clean and Review Code personally</li><li><strike>Clean Text Placeholders</strike></li><li>Connect for auto-updates instead of downloading again and again</li><li>Plan and create how to receive feedback</li><li><strike>Create Github Repo</strike></li><li><strike>Publish to Github Releases</strike></li><li>Record How to Use it</li><li>Send to Beta Testers</li><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Publish to Instagram first</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Publish to LinkedIn</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Share to Facebook</span></li></ul><li>Plan How can I earn? Maybe allow donations.</li></ol><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div>",
    "color": "#9CCFA5",
    "updatedAt": 1789388455041,
    "alwaysOnTop": false
  }
]